{"title":"2022 SSMO Accuracy Round Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a trapezoid with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/0/1201da5496d8015043ddbcbd2ea89782fcc5a3b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB \\parallel CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" />. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/8/cd842e36ed64086a882c190267900ce65d1f7017.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/c/e9c3f07d33a288bcd77ad1ffbdb1fd242cc0e8b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/b/6db9848ba8bd242cdf903446ad639c1e8053c649.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/1/d4164af5279f09df6795ff87d95768e3f8d993b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB&lt;CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> denote the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/a/cfa38ad69fc1de38f13906dff1522f42751e0bfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle XEB=\\angle ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"141\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Accuracy_Round_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/4/3342afc41ffa948da0d892075c259e0a4378d161.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(8cm); pair A = (-23/40, sqrt(1071)/40); pair B = (73/40, sqrt(1071)/40); pair C = (4,0); pair D = (0,0); pair E = (73/64,3*sqrt(119)/64); pair X = (51/80, sqrt(1071)/40); pair Y = (-23/40, 0); pair Z = (73/40, 0);  draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); draw(B--D); draw(A--C); draw(A--Y--D,dotted+linewidth(1)); draw(B--Z,dotted+linewidth(1)); draw(X--E,dotted+linewidth(1));  dot(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NW); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,NE); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SE); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,SW); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,S); dot(&quot;$X$&quot;,X,N); dot(&quot;$Y$&quot;,Y,SW); dot(&quot;$Z$&quot;,Z,S); [/asy]\" width=\"378\" height=\"105\" /> </center><p> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> be the foot of the perpendiculars from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/d/62d4ce01800c1137f8b59f4e5de12cfea9188e61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YD = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"14\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66c4c47c949fd7e6431dd1d767a7678ac42323ff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[BZ = AY = \\sqrt{1-x^2}\\quad\\text{and}\\quad ZC=\\sqrt{4-\\left(\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\right)^2}=\\sqrt{x^2+3}.\\]\" width=\"515\" height=\"43\" /> From the Law of Sines on triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/f/fef987784a6d1bfdf205d38fc46ea7b787f3c6c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XEB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/b/62b0655ed5237d15f2a52e587321c7b61d16ec17.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sin\\angle BXE}{BE}=\\frac{\\sin\\angle XEB}{XB}\\implies\\frac{\\sin(\\angle XBE+\\angle XEB)}{BE}=\\frac{\\sin\\angle ADC}{\\frac{AB}{2}}.\\]\" width=\"540\" height=\"45\" /> Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/4/2b486880edc2f80dc47f8438c3dacb6764ef7bf6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB=DC+YD-ZC=4+x-\\sqrt{x^3+3}\\]\" width=\"337\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/a/cea7b9272168e2114ce56927d8b8178cce69fd2f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin\\angle ADC = \\sin\\angle ADY = \\frac{AY}{AD}=\\sqrt{1-x^2}.\\]\" width=\"337\" height=\"37\" /> We have  \\begin{align*} BE&amp;=\\frac{AB}{AB+CD}\\cdot BD\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{AB}{AB+CD}\\cdot\\sqrt{DZ^2+BZ^2}\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{AB}{AB+CD}\\cdot\\sqrt{(CD-ZC)^2+BZ^2}\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{4+x-\\sqrt{x^2+3}}{8+x-\\sqrt{x^2+3}}\\cdot\\sqrt{\\left(4-\\sqrt{x^2+3}\\right)^2+\\left(\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\right)^2} \\end{align*} and  \\begin{align*} \\sin(\\angle XBE+\\angle XEB) &amp;= \\sin(\\angle BDC+\\angle ADC)\\\\ &amp;=\\sin\\angle BDC\\cdot\\cos\\angle ADC+\\cos\\angle BDC\\cdot\\sin\\angle ADC\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{BZ}{BD}\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{YD}{AD}\\right)+\\frac{DZ}{BD}\\cdot\\frac{AY}{AD}\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\cdot\\left(4-\\sqrt{x^2+3}\\right)-x\\sqrt{1-x^2}}{\\sqrt{\\left(4-\\sqrt{x^2+3}\\right)^2+\\left(\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\right)^2}}. \\end{align*} Substituting back into the Law of Sines relationship on triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/f/fef987784a6d1bfdf205d38fc46ea7b787f3c6c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XEB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />, we have \\begin{align*} \\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\cdot\\left(4-\\sqrt{x^2+3}\\right)-x\\sqrt{1-x^2}}{\\sqrt{\\left(4-\\sqrt{x^2+3}\\right)^2+\\left(\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\right)^2}}}{\\frac{4+x-\\sqrt{x^2+3}}{8+x-\\sqrt{x^2+3}}\\cdot\\sqrt{\\left(4-\\sqrt{x^2+3}\\right)^2+\\left(\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\right)^2}}&amp;=\\frac{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}{\\frac{4+x-\\sqrt{x^3+3}}{2}}\\implies\\\\ \\frac{\\left(4-\\sqrt{x^2+3}\\right)-x}{\\frac{1}{8+x-\\sqrt{x^2+3}}\\cdot\\left(\\left(4-\\sqrt{x^2+3}\\right)^2+\\left(\\sqrt{1-x^2}\\right)^2\\right)}&amp;=2\\implies\\\\ \\left((4-x)-\\sqrt{x^2+3}\\right)\\left((8+x)-\\sqrt{x^2+3}\\right)&amp;=2\\left(4-\\sqrt{x^2+3}\\right)^2+2(1-x^2)\\implies\\\\ 4\\sqrt{x^2+3}&amp;=4x+5\\implies\\\\ x=\\frac{23}{40}. \\end{align*} So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/a/e5a108f64e03ccf50996e053ef0a76cd550cf236.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB=4+x-\\sqrt{x^{2}+3}=4+\\frac{23}{40}-\\frac{73}{40}=\\frac{11}{4}\\implies 11+4=\\boxed{15}.\\]\" width=\"505\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018021959\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.014 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.025 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 132/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6230/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26198:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018021959 and revision id 280152. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}